# Docker build context for src/Flow.Silo/Dockerfile - context root is the REPOSITORY ROOT
# (see that Dockerfile's header comment for why). This trims the context to what a Flow.Silo
# image build actually needs: no git metadata, no local build output that could shadow a
# clean in-container restore/build, no unrelated tooling/docs/test trees.

# Local build output - never wanted inside the build context; the Dockerfile always does its
# own restore/build/publish, so a stale host bin/obj would only risk contaminating that.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
coverage/
artifacts/

# VCS / IDE / editor / local tooling state
.git/
.gitnexus/
.vs/
.vscode/
.claude/
.editorconfig

# Docs, scripts, and tooling not needed to build or run the image
docs/
scripts/
*.md

# Test projects - never referenced by Flow.Silo, no reason to enter the build context
src/Flow.Grains.Tests/
src/Flow.Grains.Tests.Integration/
src/Flow.Grains.Tests.Utils/

# devops pipeline/compose definitions aren't part of the application image
devops/
